      "description": "Dejima was a fan-shaped artificial island built in 1636 that served as Japan's only window to the Western world during the isolation period (1641–1859). Today, meticulously restored warehouses, residences, and exhibits recreate the Dutch trading post where East met West.",
      "highlights": [
        "Reconstructed Dutch trading post buildings",
